title: Close Project and quieter pickers
intro: File, Close Project returns to the start; Add Component describes a component only when asked.
project: Platformer | Quick Close

chapter: Describing a component | The list stays readable
create: Sprite
rename: Slime
say: Here's a new sprite. Let's look at what it could become.
addlist
explain: addlist:list | Names, uncovered | Hovering a component's name no longer pops a tooltip over the rows below it, so the list stays easy to read.
explain: addlist:item:Patrol | The info mark | Each row has a small info mark on its right. Rest the mouse on it, and the description appears.
type: patr
explain: addlist:blurb | Or select it | The selected component is also described in a line under the list, so the keyboard gets it too.
key: Escape

chapter: Closing the project | Back to the start
say: Done with this project? File, Close Project puts the editor back as it was before any project was open.
menu: File > Close Project
expectproject: none
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Nothing open | The scene, its panels and everything the project held are let go. Open or create a project to carry on.
